+
+### Due times (enabled with `DUE_TIMES=on`)
+
+Every returned ticket includes `due`, an ISO UTC timestamp fixed at creation. Default response hours are urgent 4, high 24, normal 72, low 168, configurable with `DUE_HOURS_<PRIORITY>`. Changing priority does not move due. Existing tickets receive a persisted deadline from their creation time on upgrade.
+
+`GET /tickets?overdue=true` selects open and in-progress tickets whose due time has strictly passed. It combines with status, priority, assignee, limit and cursor. `overdue=false` leaves the deadline unrestricted; other values return 400 while enabled. When disabled, the parameter is ignored and due is absent from responses.
